---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Hamdi Laadhari"
  description="How h4md1.fr handles analytics and cookies: Google Analytics only loads after an explicit opt-in, and nothing is sold or shared."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <main id="main" class="prose">
    <div class="wrap prose__wrap">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="hm-paper hm-label hm-label--mono hm-tilt-l">PRIVACY</p>
        <h1 class="hm-headline">
          <span class="hm-paper hm-label hm-label--display strip-lg hm-tilt-r1">WHAT THIS SITE MEASURES</span>
        </h1>

        <div class="hm-paper card hm-tilt-l1">
          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            This site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand which sections visitors actually read. Analytics is a
            non-essential measurement under CNIL guidance, so the Google tag is not present in the page and downloads
            nothing until you press <strong>Accept analytics</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Declining sets the same choice. Either way your answer is remembered on this device so the question is asked
            once, not on every page view.
          </p>

          <h2>What is measured</h2>
          <p>
            Page views, referrer, and which links get clicked — for example whether the CV button or a project link is
            used. This is aggregate traffic data used to decide what to keep on the site.
          </p>

          <h2>What is not</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>No advertising or ad-personalisation cookies.</li>
            <li>No cross-site tracking, no remarketing audiences.</li>
            <li>No data sold, rented, or shared with third-party advertisers.</li>
            <li>No advertising ID, no fingerprinting.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Who receives it</h2>
          <p>
            Google Ireland Limited, as Google's EU establishment. Aggregate data may be processed in the United States
            under Google's standard contractual clauses.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can opt out of Google Analytics for the whole web at
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
              >tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a
            >.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR you can ask what data is held about you, correct it, or have it erased. Write to
            <a href="mailto:contact@h4md1.fr">contact@h4md1.fr</a> and it will be answered.
          </p>

          <h2>Change your mind</h2>
          <p>
            Clear this site's data in your browser to see the choice again, or email me and I will reset it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a class="hm-button hm-button--primary" href="/">Back to the story →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
